      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6i3",
          "text": "Victims of pedestrian accidents in Colorado often experience injuries that cause pain, immobility, scarring, and diminished enjoyment of life – in addition to expensive medical bills and lost wages. You may be eligible for compensation for all of these losses and more with a pedestrian accident claim in Thornton.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6i6",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6i5",
          "text": "What Types of Compensation Are Available for a Pedestrian Injury?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6i9",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6i7",
          "text": "Colorado law allows injured accident victims to recover financial compensation (also known as damages) for both economic and noneconomic losses. Economic damages are the financial costs of the accident. They are also known as specific losses, as they come with a quantifiable monetary value. Noneconomic damages are intangible losses and are not as easy to calculate. You may be eligible for the following damages in your pedestrian accident case:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
